# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"
msgstr "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every job runs at one size — `S`, `M` or `L`. If you select a size that's too small, the job is rejected.  If you select a size that's larger\n"
"than needed and it runs on a bigger compute profile than the work requires. See\n"
"[Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) for how sizes work in general.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tumatakbo ang bawat job sa iisang size — `S`, `M` o `L`. Kung masyadong maliit ang size na pipiliin mo, ire-reject ang job.  Kung mas malaki ang pipiliin mong size kaysa kailangan, tatakbo ito sa mas malaking compute profile kaysa sa kailangan ng gawain. Tingnan ang\n"
"[Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) para sa pangkalahatang paliwanag kung paano gumagana ang mga size.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The size comes from two properties of your model: how many variables it has, and\n"
"how densely they interact — the fraction of all variable pairs that appear together\n"
"in a term of the objective or of a constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakabatay ang size sa dalawang katangian ng model mo: kung ilan ang mga variable nito, at\n"
"kung gaano kasiksik ang interaksyon ng mga ito — ang bahagi ng lahat ng pares ng variable na magkasamang lumalabas\n"
"sa isang term ng objective o ng isang constraint.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Size | Smallest size for variables and interaction density | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `S` | At most 50 variables and density at most 0.1 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | At most 100 variables and density at most 0.25 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
"| `L` | either above the `M` bound | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Size | Pinakamaliit na size para sa mga variable at interaction density | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `S` | Hanggang 50 variable at density na hanggang 0.1 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | Hanggang 100 variable at density na hanggang 0.25 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
"| `L` | lampas sa hangganan ng `M` | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A model must fit **both** bounds of a size, which is why a small but tightly coupled\n"
"model can be `L`: ten variables all coupled to each other is a density of 1.0. These\n"
"are the same bounds for every optimization function, so a size means the same\n"
"difficulty of model whichever one you call.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dapat pasok ang isang model sa **parehong** hangganan ng isang size, kaya puwedeng maging `L` ang maliit pero mahigpit ang pagkakaugnay na\n"
"model: ang sampung variable na magkakaugnay lahat ay may density na 1.0. Pareho ang\n"
"mga hangganang ito para sa bawat optimization function, kaya magkapareho ang\n"
"hirap ng model sa isang size, alinman ang tawagin mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two things raise the density more than they appear to:\n"
msgstr "May dalawang bagay na mas nagpapataas ng density kaysa sa inaakala:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A term over more than two variables couples every pair of them.** A term in\n"
"four variables contributes all six pairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang isang term na sumasaklaw sa higit sa dalawang variable ay nag-uugnay sa bawat pares nila.** Ang isang term na may\n"
"apat na variable ay nag-aambag ng lahat ng anim na pares.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A constraint counts as the penalty that replaces it on hardware.** Squaring the\n"
"constraint couples every pair of variables in it, so a one-hot constraint over\n"
"four variables also contributes all six pairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang constraint ay binibilang bilang ang penalty na pumapalit dito sa hardware.** Ang pag-square sa\n"
"constraint ay nag-uugnay sa bawat pares ng variable dito, kaya ang one-hot constraint sa\n"
"apat na variable ay nag-aambag din ng lahat ng anim na pares.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default is `M`, used when a job does not request a size.\n"
msgstr "Ang default ay `M`, na ginagamit kapag walang hiniling na size ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Users can also read the mapping off the function itself with `optimizer.sizes_map`, and\n"
"the size used when a job does not ask for one with `optimizer.default_size`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mababasa rin ng mga user ang mapping mula mismo sa function gamit ang `optimizer.sizes_map`, at\n"
